pe":"block","kind":"notebook-content","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Another drawback is that if you commit a file to source control, diffs are usually on a per line basis. Change one element of the data in a long reshape expression, and the whole line gets flagged as changed, which complicates life for a reviewer.","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"rCPbyl2erd"}],"key":"vLlu9xIbTM"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"One of the main new features of the v20 release of Dyalog was ","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"Iudikwq6Fu"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Array Notation","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"oEXnGxQhZq"}],"key":"ftfE1ztlsa"},{"type":"text","value":" (APLAN) -- a different way to lay out array literals in code (it has other purposes, too; for later). Whilst the feature is new, it’s been a long time coming. Phil Last’s ","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"PHBS1obPFr"},{"type":"link","url":"https://www.dyalog.com/uploads/conference/dyalog15/presentations/U07_APL_Array_Notation.pdf","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"presentation","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"m0LmRMLf1l"}],"urlSource":"https://www.dyalog.com/uploads/conference/dyalog15/presentations/U07_APL_Array_Notation.pdf","key":"VwQ1bCJira"},{"type":"text","value":" at the 2015 Dyalog User Meeting, and his subsequent ","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"ZSmNlh9CBL"},{"type":"link","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20250819080522/https://archive.vector.org.uk/art10501450","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"article","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"S2YhrFypHY"}],"urlSource":"https://web.archive.org/web/20250819080522/https://archive.vector.org.uk/art10501450","key":"DRnsP7gJSZ"},{"type":"text","value":" in Vector are arguably the original blueprints for Dyalog v20, even if similar ideas have been floating around the APL community since the dawn of time.","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"UMeRDMjPED"}],"key":"LZte6977vl"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"We’ll be using APLAN extensively, and the purpose of this chapter is to introduce the concepts sufficiently in order for you to follow along. We’ll return to APLAN in more depth in the namespaces chapter later on.","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"key":"NfKQ1mLbp6"}],"key":"bAj4YBvguj"}],"key":"F6fAeBo8C3"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-content","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Diamonds and newlines","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"H5HXB3ss3J"}],"identifier":"diamonds-and-newlines","label":"Diamonds and newlines","html_id":"diamonds-and-newlines","implicit":true,"key":"bO4p6OkseC"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"APL has two syntactically equivalent forms of statement separators: newlines, and the diamond symbol, ","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"jnC0LeL1YM"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"⋄","position":{"s